📅 Day 49 – Handling GET & POST Requests in Servlets

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on handling client requests in servlets using GET and POST methods. The mentor explained how data is sent from the client to the server and how these methods differ in terms of usage and security.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ GET Method
Data is sent through URL parameters
Suitable for retrieving data
Limited data size
Less secure (data visible in URL)
2️⃣ POST Method
Data is sent in the request body
Suitable for sending sensitive data
No size limitation
More secure than GET
3️⃣ Servlet Methods
doGet() → Handles GET requests
doPost() → Handles POST requests

These methods process client requests and generate responses.

🔹 Practical Work

During the practice session, I:

Created HTML forms to send user input
Developed servlets to handle GET and POST requests
Retrieved form data using request object
Displayed output in the browser

This helped me understand how user input is transmitted and processed in web applications.